{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen","id":1437939,"title":"My (kind of opposite) problem with something else in chargen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-03-04T04:27:00-08:00","id":1437939,"title":"My (kind of opposite) problem with something else in chargen","content":"I felt like this was more of an aside to the main issue, and probably most people won't even consider it to be one since I'm\u2026 sort of weird about this stuff, I guess.<br /> <br /> I thought of it more like the flipside of what happens when you <i>don't</i> make the 5/5 character regardless of concept or guidelines.<br /> <br /> Also, these are more ramble-y and possibly way, way off \u2013 which is why I went for a separate post.<br /> <br /> <b>Supposition 1:</b><br /> Exalted is a game where traits have dot ratings and those dot ratings have narrative descriptions, the rating has &quot;story&quot; meaning in terms of gauging the character's traits in comparison with the rest of the world.<br /> <br /> For example, having a Craft (Painting) rating of 1 and a Melee rating of 5 define the character as being an amateur painter and a legendary master swordsman, respectively.<br /> The character's Appearance 3 means he's handsome and his Backing, Influence and Resources ratings tell us he's the captain of the local town guard and a respectable member of the local community, whose word carries some weight locally, and with a generous government stipend.<br /> His Allies and Retainers ratings tell us about the hotheaded-but-loyal guardswoman who became his most trusted companion, and the shady cat-eyed man who owes the captain his life and swore to serve him in secret until he could repay the Captain the favor\u2026<br /> <br /> <b><i>Important:</i></b> We are told that a rating of 2 in a trait is average while rating 5 is a very <i>rare</i> thing that defines the level of a legendary master.<br /> <br /> In other words, specific numbers <i>mean specific things.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Supposition 2:</b><br /> Exalted is also a game where dot ratings are used as dice pools for actions and as <i>&quot;Must Be This Tall&quot;</i> requirements to purchase Charms.<br /> <br /> In order to be competent in any particular action, one needs to have a high dice pool.<br /> A pool of 4 or 5 dice is not acceptable for actions that are supposed to be part of a character's core competencies, especially on actions that tend to be opposed or resisted with surpassingly high and higher numbers, penalties and difficulties.<br /> <br /> For example, if your character is supposed to be The Warrior, you cannot just put one dot in Brawl or Melee and expect to be The Warrior of <i>anything</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Problem: </b><br /> Say we want to make a character.<br /> &quot;Daring young farm girl&quot; is a listed concept from the Dawn Caste's description page in the core rulebook, so let's take that as an example.<br /> <br /> We got an idea brewing, picturing this young peasant with the classic &quot;village gets destroyed by\u2026&quot; opener. Enraged and driven, she fights back, yada, yada, yada.<br /> You might've seen a similar scene somewhere, that one time, you get the picture.<br /> <br /> So we get to the character creation part of character creation\u2026<br /> <br /> If you're like me, you want to build the character in a way that makes sense for the concept, trying to give the character traits that are logical things for her to have \u2013 but the things that are logical for the character's traits on paper are naturally things that put us in the problem from the end of Supposition 2:<br /> She's a peasant, she did not grow up mastering melee combat skills.<br /> <br /> So if we want her to be <i>The Warrior of the Group</i> (Dawn Caste, after all), you have to stretch and round some mental corners if you're going to stick to &quot;x number of dots in y means z&quot;.<br /> <br /> She may have been a bit of a tomboy, but could she have gotten Athletics 3 and Dodge 3?<br /> Remember, that is a level which, according to the core book, means that our character's &quot;<b>training</b> in the Ability surpasses the competence expected even of professional&quot;.<br /> <br /> A lot of things that would be important for the character to have, for example Charms, require things like <i>Melee <b>4</b></i>, which would make her an expert veteran.<br /> <br /> I'm aware that character creation doesn't represent the character at the moment of Exaltation but picks things up after she's had some time to start to get to grips with her Essence and maybe hone her abilities a bit.<br /> I'm also aware that you can justify an exalt attaining a higher level in a trait through talent and their inherent heroic excellence, but we want to stay faithful to our concept, which suggests starting with low ability dots.<br /> <br /> Yes, we're supposed to be a fucking <i>Exalt</i> and that calls for some <i>&quot;oh, this young character is already swinging a sword at the level of my best swordsman!&quot;</i>, but this also that breaks away from <i>&quot;if you're an apprentice sculptor, </i><b>this one dot</b><i> is the level of apprentice sculptors&quot;</i> ratings \u2013 and those same ability rating descriptors are there <i>for you</i>, to represent <i>your character</i>.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Important: </i></b>We are told that inborn talent is represented through Attributes, and that Abilities represent <b><i>&quot;training, education and experience&quot;.</i></b><br /> <br /> This is exactly my problem with the system \u2013 does it want me to accurately build a young farmer or does it want me to build a character that will be efficient in combat?<br /> <br /> Exalted is a game that's supposed to be about playing mythic heroes capable of <i>300</i>'ing their way through armies \u2013 but it's also a game that makes you aware of how your Melee rating compares to both your concept and the NPC's around you and keeps insisting that you don't need to be mathematically efficient, while at the same time it puts up a Mathematical Efficiency Paywall on the kind of Charms you kinda-sorta <i>need</i> for your character.<br /> <br /> Yes, you can Defend Other without War Lion Stance and you can maybe get away with doing it at Melee 1 (and a high Dexterity) if you Stunt and also throw an Excellency into the mix, but I won't go into an Efficiency argument here \u2013 the point is that in order to get the magical ability to Defend Other while also doing other stuff (fighting, presumably) you need X dots in Melee and in this case, the rating of a master and veteran.<br /> <br /> The specific descriptions tied to specific levels of traits in the system also kind of forget that this is a dice <i>pool</i> system.<br /> So a character with Melee 4 is considered more skilled at Melee than a character with Melee 3.<br /> BUT the character with Melee 4 might have a Dexterity of 2 while the character with Melee 3 might have Dexterity 5 and also a Specialty in their Melee trait.<br /> <br /> This is the reason that when the book declares that a rating of one dot in a given Ability means XYZ, it essentially <i>lies</i> because that one dot doesn't exist in a vacuum \u2013 it's attached to an Attribute and possibly a Specialty and other traits such as Accuracy or situational modifiers.<br /> <br /> There is no way that a character with Charisma 2 and Performance 3 is &quot;of higher skill&quot; than a character with Charisma 5 and Performance 1.<br /> <br /> The book can claim all it wants that the average soldier has Melee 2, but does the average soldier also have Dexterity 2 or is it 3?<br /> Can you tell the difference in skill level between a mortal soldier with Dex 4+Melee 2, versus another soldier with Dex 3+Melee 3?<br /> <br /> <b>Bringing it Back to Chargen</b><br /> <br /> The flipside of the issue with chargen, being how easy it is to make a character with 5/5's, is what happens when you specifically try to follow the book's guidelines and make a character's stats reflect their concept.<br /> <br /> In other words, a problem with character creation is that following the book's very own guidelines and trying your hardest to <i>not min-max or power-game it</i> is simply <i>not a thing that you can do</i>.<br /> <br /> We don't live in a world where you point to your rating in Occult and say that &quot;this is the level I felt to be representative of an inexperienced shaman who inherited a great mystical power and finds themselves fighting demons to protect their clan&quot; \u2013 we live in a world where you need a minimum of 3 in Occult to gain access to the Charms that let you actually do that, and practically speaking you'd need more of a 4 or 5 if you want to actually be good at any of it and not just inflict ping on NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T06:30:15-08:00","id":1437951,"title":"","content":"Opening a lock is Difficulty 1.<br /> <br /> Opening a First Age lock is difficulty 4.<br /> <br /> Dex 3, Larceny 3, a 2-dice stunt and a 6-dice Excellency opens that First Age lock 92% of the time.<br /> Dex 2 and Larceny 2 is doing it 75% of the time. 89% of the time with Exceptional Tools. 96% of the time if they spend Willpower as well. <br /> <br /> 4-5 dice is <i>fine</i>.<br /> <br /> What else... Resisting lava is difficulty 5. If you can throw 5 dice at that then with a stunt and excellency you succeed 73% of the time.<br /> <br /> Hitting an elite soldier in combat? Difficulty 5. You have Dex 2 Melee 2? 73% chance of hitting. <br /> <br /> You want to convince the Resolve 4 Snakeman Merchant to give you a discount? Charisma 2 Presence 2 gives you a 75% success rate. 89% with Willpower.<br /> <br /> You don't need 5s.<br /> <br /> The average mortal soldier doesn't have Dexterity and Melee because these are system abstractions. They're player facing mechanics. They have &quot;Chopping Sword: Accuracy 7&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Solars started reappearing five years ago. If you want to say that your Farm Girl Dawn has gone from Melee 2 to Melee 3 immediately on Exalting then bumped up to Melee 5 over the last five years, I don't have a problem with that.<br /> <br /> But you don't need Melee 5 to be an effective warrior.<br /> <br /> Moreover, the Charm minimums enforce rarity. Iron Whirlwind Technique is not something every random Solar can do. It's rare. You don't <i>need</i> it.<br /> <br /> You don't need Larceny 4 to make a disguise. You need Larceny 4 to make a magical disguise so good that it cannot be defeated. Where does your magic come from? Your training and skill. You need to be a cut above the veteran master of disguise to make a flawlessly impenetrable disguise because that charm is the mechanical representation of your magical skill. If you only have Larceny 2, the skill of an average professional, how in the heck do you propose that your average professional disguises be flawlessly impenetrable?<br /> <br /> You don't need War Lion Stance to Defend Other. You can Flurry your Defend Other with an Attack at Melee 0. No special ability required. Dex 3 Melee 3 and a medium weapon, and you're hitting a zombie 72% of the time with the flurry penalty without stunting or using an excellency. Stunt and Excellency and you can hit a Bride of Ahlat 79% of the time. If you are an exceptional warrior, you might have access to specialist magic that makes that tactic more efficient, but the numbers of the game mean you don't need Melee 4 if you want to use Defend Other. The magical defend other power requires the abilities of an exceptional veteran because it doesn't exist. War Lion Stance isn't an upgrade you plug into your character. It's the mechanical representation of having a character <i>so good</i> at Melee fighting that they can seamlessly defend their allies as a casual afterthought whilst dunking on their enemies. A swordfighter so skilled that deflecting blows aimed at their ward doesn't impact on their own offense or defense <i>at all</i>. That doesn't sound like a skill belonging to a merely average swordfighter. That sounds like the skill of an absolute legend.<br /> <br /> Spirit Detecting Glance is Occult 1. Spirit Cutting Attack (and most spirits need to materialise before they can do anything to you) is Occult 2. You could totally play an apprentice shaman whofights demons with Occult 1/2. (Or you could take Occult 3 and just say the master you inherited your power from was Occult 5. So even though you are mighty by the standards of normal folks, you know you still have a way to go.)<br /> <br /> The Bride uses the Five Point Palm Exploding Heart Technique exactly once. The rest of the film she uses her MA 3 techniques.<br /> <br /> Now I would encourage you to give your Farm Girl Dawn Melee 5 if that was her thing. It's not a fun, unique idea to play a Melee 1 Dawn. But she doesn't need Athletics 5. Let her have her tomboy Athletics 3. And if you think Dodge 3 is too high... well give her Dodge 2. The sky won't fall in on you. The game will still work. You'll still be able to dodge lava flows (assuming Dexterity 3 and the Excellency).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 03-04-2021, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T07:32:17-08:00","id":1437956,"title":"","content":"Also your base exalted characters are supposed to be a bit exceptional in at least some areas. You get 28 ability dots, you get 8 bonus dots in your primary attribute, you simply can\u2019t spend all of those and have a character with dots representative of a regular farmhand. <br /> <br /> Also as an aside I think the attribute and ability descriptions are okay. True somebody with five in every physical stat is likely to beat a 2/2 average professional soldier even if he has no dots in combat abilities, just through sheer physicality, but he\u2019s still completely untrained for combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T07:53:10-08:00","id":1437958,"title":"","content":"There's a pretty common trope in the genres Exalted pulls from of the accidental expert. Learning Shaolin kung-fu by way of construction techniques in Return to the 36th Chamber, the ancient family clothes washing techniques actually being a masterful grasp of Eagle Claw style in Dreadnought. Goblin Slayer being so absurdly skilled and clever entirely from slaying goblins that he can use goblin slaying techniques on things that aren't goblins.<br /> <br /> With your farm girl example, it'd be extremely easy to explain away a very high combat Ability by having to constantly deal with pests. Having to throw rocks at the pests stealing the grain being really similar to throwing a lead ball through someone's eye, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T09:03:27-08:00","id":1437965,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen#post1437939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is exactly my problem with the system \u2013 does it want me to accurately build a young farmer or does it want me to build a character that will be efficient in combat?.</div> </div> </div> </div>It mostly depends on what you and your group considers fun. <br /> <br /> Some people like to start as epic level characters while others feel they've been cheated out of a part of their character's journey.<br /> <br /> In addition some Storytellers build their chronicles with a fixed endpoint and follow a loose 3 or 5 act structure before the curtain calls, others are happy with a largely episodic tale that continues until nobody wants to play anymore. The latter is more favourable to a young farmer coming to terms with being a Dawn Caste and training her skills while the former typically favours immediate mastery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T09:11:01-08:00","id":1437967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1437958#post1437958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With your farm girl example, it'd be extremely easy to explain away a very high combat Ability by having to constantly deal with pests. Having to throw rocks at the pests stealing the grain being really similar to throwing a lead ball through someone's eye, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I used to bullseye womp rats in my T-16 back home...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T10:59:46-08:00","id":1437983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1437958#post1437958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With your farm girl example, it'd be extremely easy to explain away a very high combat Ability by having to constantly deal with pests. Having to throw rocks at the pests stealing the grain being really similar to throwing a lead ball through someone's eye, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does that equate to a high rating based on the narrative descriptions of them? A young shepherd might defend their flock from predators with a sling, and as part of their livelihood maybe take that to a 2. Where does a 3, let alone more come in?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1437965#post1437965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some people like to start as epic level characters while others feel they've been cheated out of a part of their character's journey.<br /> <br /> In addition some Storytellers build their chronicles with a fixed endpoint and follow a loose 3 or 5 act structure before the curtain calls, others are happy with a largely episodic tale that continues until nobody wants to play anymore. The latter is more favourable to a young farmer coming to terms with being a Dawn Caste and training her skills while the former typically favours immediate mastery.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that the book doesn't really acknowledge this is basically the problem though.<br /> <br /> If the book basically said there's two &quot;core&quot; ways to play Exalted, and advised you figure out which your group was doing and then build with that in mind - even without changing the numbers available to characters - there wouldn't be the same sort of disconnect the OP is bringing up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T12:18:30-08:00","id":1437998,"title":"","content":"I have previously proposed:<br /> <br /> Lower all Ability requirements of all Ability-based Charms by 1, except for the ones that are already at 1 (keep those at 1), and the ones at 5 with a prerequisite that is also a 5 (keep those at 5).<br /> <br /> I think this would help a bit. People have disagreed with this suggestion, but I don't think anyone has explained that it would, like, break the game.<br /> <br /> Other than that, Solars are supposed to be able to learn things super fast. She could have easily gone up a dot or two in Melee in the &quot;Enraged and driven, she fights back, yada, yada, yada&quot; step if one of the things she was driven to do was <i>train for battle</i>, and she kept it up for <i>a few days</i> after Exalting.<br /> <br /> The idea of being a badass through training is central to the idea of the Solar Exalted - if you want to play a farmhand who never trained to fight and is still an awesome fighter, you can play a Lunar.<br /> <br /> Finally, you don't <i>need</i> these Charms to play a badass. If your players and ST agree on &quot;My Athletics 2, Dodge 2, Melee 2, Resistance 2 barely-trained farm girl is the strongest combatant in the group&quot; you can achieve that, rules as written, and beat plenty of enemies in the core book. You'll probably have a lot of fun in those fights, and in growing your character over time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T13:03:56-08:00","id":1438004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1437983#post1437983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does that equate to a high rating based on the narrative descriptions of them? A young shepherd might defend their flock from predators with a sling, and as part of their livelihood maybe take that to a 2. Where does a 3, let alone more come in?</div> </div> </div> </div>From getting that good at it. Not everyone benefits equally from the same kind and amount of practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T13:59:07-08:00","id":1438017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1437998#post1437998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People have disagreed with this suggestion, but I don't think anyone has explained that it would, like, break the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have quibbles with the specific implementation, but I'm completely behind the general concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The idea of being a badass through training is central to the idea of the Solar Exalted - if you want to play a farmhand who never trained to fight and is still an awesome fighter, you can play a Lunar. </div> </div> </div>I think it's a minor but important difference: being a badass through skill is central to the idea of Solars. Training is how you get skill obviously, but Solars aren't built around the process buy the end result. Which is why a lot of people pump up a rating by 1 or 2 based on just being innately awesome and it doesn't mess with the Solar-ness of the character.<br /> <br /> I'm also fairly confident from the OP's post that they're aware of how Attributes can elevate a character with low Ability scores to higher level performance; but that only adds to the disconnect of making a character by letting concept dictate the dots vs. acknowledging all the ways the system encourages you to take ratings for more mechanical reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other than that, Solars are supposed to be able to learn things super fast. She could have easily gone up a dot or two in Melee in the &quot;Enraged and driven, she fights back, yada, yada, yada&quot; step if one of the things she was driven to do was <i>train for battle</i>, and she kept it up for <i>a few days</i> after Exalting. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438004#post1438004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From getting that good at it. Not everyone benefits equally from the same kind and amount of practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>This already addressed in the OP as a violation of Supposition 1. The concept is not &quot;former farm girl now rebel warrior,&quot; but, &quot;daring young farm girl.&quot; as is a suggestion in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T14:31:09-08:00","id":1438021,"title":"","content":"Luke Skywalker is a farm boy.<br /> <br /> He's also one of the greatest crack pilots in the galaxy because he trains every day running target drills that are too difficult for a computer to pull off.<br /> <br /> Will Turner is a blacksmith's apprentice. He drills for three hours every day with the swords he forges.<br /> <br /> David was a sheep herder. But he practiced killing wolves with his sling then was blessed by God with supranatural talent.<br /> <br /> There's this kid called &quot;Clark&quot; who grew up on this farm in kansas...<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Most tattooine moisture farmers aren't the son of Darth Vader. But Star Wars isn't the story of the average farm boy. It's the story of an exceptional hero.<br /> <br /> But Luke isn't, as well as being an ace pilot, also the greatest lothario in the galaxy, and a hyperbrain engineer who upgrades the millennium falcon, and an expert lightsaber duelist, and a champion code breaker, and a renown doctor. Even in terms of his force abilities, he's not the greatest jedi in the world. He's a super special protagonist, hero of his own story though -- hasn't even been to flight school yet casually outflies the greatest pilots in the star wars.<br /> <br /> Average Farm Girl being the greatest swordfighter in the world is incongruous. Absolutely.<br /> <br /> Solar Protagonist being the greatest swordfighter in the world is probably fine. Especially as it literally takes two weeks for a PC to train from Melee 1 to Melee 5 without a tutor.<br /> <br /> You're the hero of the story. You're playing Son Goku. You are the amazing one-in-a-generation prodigy, chosen by the king of heaven.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong. If all the players are on board, you can get a lot of milage out of &quot;normal person gains Solar powers&quot;. But Exalted is kinda about playing someone exceptional (whether born, become, or thrust upon).<br /> <br /> I mean... are you saying you can't take a 5?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438004#post1438004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From getting that good at it. Not everyone benefits equally from the same kind and amount of practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this.<br /> <br /> My sister and I took guitar and piano lessons side by side for three years. She rocks the guitar but after three years struggled with chopsticks. I can only play power chords on guitar but can play piano.<br /> <br /> Different folks are good at different stuff. Different folks given the same opportunities will have different results. Because people are different.<br /> <br /> <i>Your</i> Farm Girl can have different stats to an NPC farm girl.<br /> <br /> Now if you're going to try to tell me that your southern farm girl who's never seen the ocean has Sail 5, I'm going to raise an eyebrow. But you wanna say your Dawn got Thrown 5 but hunting rats in the cornstacks? Well all I can say is, you must be playing some kind of exceptional hero - a gifted one-in-a-million natural warrior - to get world class combat skills like that! Oh wait, you are!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 03-04-2021, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T14:42:17-08:00","id":1438027,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Please don't bring up the omni-competence at character generation thing again, FYI. The last thread was locked for a reason.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T15:42:29-08:00","id":1438035,"title":"","content":"To elaborate on what I said earlier, I attempted to make a brave young farm girl following the character creation rules, sticking as close as possible to &quot;only the Abilities a brave young farm girl could take, with a very small amount of post-Exaltation training giving a +1&quot; while also being a capable warrior and a playable character. This is what I got:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Athletics 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Awareness 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Brawl 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Craft (Farm Tools) 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dodge 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Integrity 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Larceny 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Medicine 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Melee 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Performance (Singing) 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Presence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Resistance 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ride 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Socialize 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stealth 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Survival 3</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Athletics: Graceful Crane Stance</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Athletics: Monkey Leap Technique</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Brawl: Fists of Iron Technique</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Integrity: Enduring Mental Toughness</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Integrity: Stubborn Boar Technique</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Medicine: Ailment-Rectifying Method</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Melee: Excellent Strike</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Melee: One Weapon, Two Blows</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Melee: Dipping Swallow Defense</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Resistance: Ox-Body Technique</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Resistance: Durability of Oak Meditation</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Resistance: Iron Skin Concentration</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ride: Master Horseman\u2019s Technique</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Survival: Hardship-Surviving Mendicant Spirit</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Survival: Friendship with Animals Approach</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Strength 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dexterity 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stamina 4</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Appearance 1<br /> Charisma 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Manipulation 3</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Intelligence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Perception 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wits 4</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> To make this character the group's warrior, you would have to ask the other players to take at most a 2 in combat Abilities, and no or almost no combat Charms. But if the group wanted to do that, you could.<br /> <br /> I haven't tested this specific character, but my understanding from previous fights I've seen is that there is a lot of enemy monsters she could wreck, as well as small battlegroups of mortal (i.e. she could take on dozens of people). If the Storyteller wanted to allow it, she could be a total badass. And she would grow even stronger over time.<br /> <br /> Was whichever dev or original writer who wrote that thinking you would build your character like this when they put that entry in the Dawn character concepts list? Probably not - they were probably thinking more like Eric Minton and John Doe's suggestions of a farm girl/boy who displays exceptional talent like some noted fictional characters. But I think the system would support you if you wanted to do it this way.<br /> <br /> (I hope that bringing up a concrete example will take this thread further from the old thread, and help it be generally less argumentative. If not, I hope it at least doesn't make anything worse.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T15:59:37-08:00","id":1438036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438035#post1438035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If not, I hope it at least doesn't make anything worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've done the worst thing I could possibly imagine: now I want to run a game for this character. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What's her name?<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> I think if you're going to run a character like that, you're probably better off with minimal niche protection. Have every character be about as capable in combat (or just a shade less: Dex 3, Melee 2 and two Melee Charms compared to the Dawn's +1 Dex and extra Melee Charm), else run minimal combat scenes. Because whilst you could have Dawn, the Farm Girl Dawn Caste, fight a Bride of Ahlat whilst the rest of the circle fights brigands, there's not a lot of compression room to play with here. And combat takes a long time and you don't want the other players feeling sidelined.<br /> <br /> In a game where the Dawn has Melee 5 and half-a-dozen Melee Charms, the Twilight can take Melee 2, Excellent Strike and Dipping Swallow Defence and there's still a ton of stuff the Twilight can fight (and utterly wreckface dominating). Whilst if the Dawn is Melee 2 with three Charms and the Twilight is Melee 0 with no Charms... there's not a lot of stuff the Twilight can fight.<br /> <br /> But yeah... that works. It feels better suited to a game where all the characters are generalists because I think it'd be hard to stand-out with that build... but it works.<br /> <br /> Like... the Power Rangers. Jason is a better fighter than Zach. He's literally Zach's teacher. But when they suit up and fight Zach holds his own and kicks ass -- it's not like Jason is in a totally different league. That's kinda what I'd expect with this Dawn Farm Girl. Sure, she's the best fighter in the group, but not by some insurmountable margin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 03-04-2021, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T20:56:00-08:00","id":1438065,"title":"","content":"1) This is why when I ran Exalted games, I ran <i>Mortal</i> campaigns. I know I sound like a broken record, but ........ guys. <i><b>Guys</b></i>. <i>So much easier</i>. And, dare I say it, more fun?<br /> <br /> Plus, when people play mortals, they, at least in my experience, seem to be <i>much</i>more willing to take 2s and 3s, or hell even 1s, than when they play Exalted.<br /> <br /> Lower ratings make the game more fun, not less<br /> <br /> 2) The main reason I got away from Exalted is because there is <i>very</i> little official actual help, either for the players to build characters or for the ST to build a world.<br /> <br /> The D&amp;D Players Handbook had sections on <i>how to play a character</i>, and how to <i>design a character</i><i>. </i>The D&amp;D DM's Guide was an <i><b>entire book</b></i> on how to build campaigns, build worlds, build individual dungeons, how to have PCs mesh with NPCs in the world, how to adapt combat and other encounters for your party<br /> <br /> Now, <u><i>yes,</i></u> D&amp;D has its own issues, but the fact of the matter is that stuff <i><b>was there</b></i>, if not from the beginning of the line then early on.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Core Rulebook should have had similar sections","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T22:00:13-08:00","id":1438074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1437983#post1437983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does that equate to a high rating based on the narrative descriptions of them? A young shepherd might defend their flock from predators with a sling, and as part of their livelihood maybe take that to a 2. Where does a 3, let alone more come in?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The fact that the book doesn't really acknowledge this is basically the problem though.<br /> <br /> If the book basically said there's two &amp;quot;core&amp;quot; ways to play Exalted, and advised you figure out which your group was doing and then build with that in mind - even without changing the numbers available to characters - there wouldn't be the same sort of disconnect the OP is bringing up.</div> </div> </div> </div>It comes in by them not having anything to compare it to. A more grounded example(ish) is Initial D. Main character was just a tofu delivery driver. Unbeknownst to him, driving the mountains of Japan in a way the tofu doesn't spill makes him among the best drift racers around. At the story's start he's got Drive 3 at absolute minimum but he just thinks he's doing a job. Someone else points out how great a racer he'd be","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T00:08:40-08:00","id":1438080,"title":"","content":"Karate kid has Daniel-san waxing the floors to become All Valley Karate Champion.<br /> Dragonball has Goku delivering milk.<br /> In Kill Bill, B- draws water from the well every morning.<br /> Luke hunts varmits. <br /> Rey scavenges wrecks for parts.<br /> Ani races pods.<br /> The Lone Wanderer learns to shoot by nailing giant mutant cockroaches with a BB gun.<br /> Jenna literally just works in a dinner. That's it. Greatest baker in the world.<br /> <br /> I mean, Rocky is an amateur boxer who has a training montage where he runs up a flight of steps.<br /> <br /> You can pretty much pick a protagonist here.<br /> <br /> It's a common trope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T01:37:13-08:00","id":1438083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438074#post1438074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It comes in by them not having anything to compare it to.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is still ignoring the premise of the situation.<br /> <br /> We all know how to apply the (kinda lazy) tricks use to explain how supposedly everyday people have insane talents in various stories.<br /> <br /> The OP isn't asking &quot;how do I write a daring farm girl to justify having a high rating in X by adding things to the concept?&quot; The OP is asking how do you stick to the concept without expanding it and still handle the pressures in the system to build your character with an eye towards higher stats.<br /> <br /> &quot;The book is wrong to offer daring farm girl as a sample concept for a Dawn, and should have done something like farm girl with unrealized potential instead,&quot; is a valid response, but it's also focusing on the example over the point.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T04:05:37-08:00","id":1438101,"title":"","content":"You don't.<br /> <br /> If you don't want to add tricks to justify being a world class combatant on your farm girl, then don't take world class stats on your farm girl. Play a build like habitableexoplanet posted for your Dawn.<br /> <br /> Your Dawn doesn't need to have Melee 5. If it doesn't make sense for your character then don't take it.<br /> <br /> You'll still be an awesome combatant that can take on the dreaded manticore, eerie ghostfishers, hundreds strong armies of zombies, combat focused demons of the first circle, wolf packs and the like with Melee 2, Excellent Strike and Dipping Swallow Defence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 03-05-2021, 07:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T04:53:11-08:00","id":1438103,"title":"","content":"I can sympathize with the argument that even if you would be okay with having lower dot ratings, the Charm prerequisites effectively force you into hypercompetence, because even though a character with Melee 2, Excellent Strike and Dipping Swallow Defense can expect to take on a wide variety of antagonists and win, it's not going to be a very mechanically interesting character to play.<br /> <br /> However, I think a solution to that is not to shrug and say &quot;ah well, I better pick Melee 5 on my freshly exalted farm girl&quot;, but to lower the stupidly high ability prerequisites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T04:55:36-08:00","id":1438104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438101#post1438101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't.<br /> <br /> If you don't want to add tricks to justify being a world class combatant on your farm girl, then don't take world class stats on your farm girl. Play a build like habitableexoplanet posted for your Dawn.<br /> <br /> Your Dawn doesn't need to have Melee 5. If it doesn't make sense for your character then don't take it.<br /> <br /> You'll still be an awesome combatant that can take on the dreaded manticore, eerie ghostfishers, hundreds strong armies of zombies, combat focused demons of the first circle, wolf packs and the like with Melee 2, Excellent Strike and Dipping Swallow Defence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. This does not, however, justify having some attributes at least at 4. Or a plethora of abilities, far more than any farmgirl rightfully should. It also doesn't have to.<br /> <br /> The daring farmgirl here isn't just a daring farmgirl. She's THE daring farmgirl chosen above so many others to carry the exaltation of the greatest deity in creation. She's special, maybe because in the month's following her exaltation she has experienced rapid growth. Or may she spent every free moment exploring, climbing trees and fallen towers of a lost civilization near her village. She's fought wolves, dodged snakes and ran from bears. She's fought the vilage bullies with her fists and constantly challenges the town's future blacksmith to arm wrestling competitions. She has a deeper well of talent than any in her village knew, because she lived a peaceful life. Until one day she didn't.<br /> <br /> The thing here is that whether she is just an important NPC or a PC, she's more than some farm girl with a bit of an adventurous spirit even before exaltation. A concept is where you start, not end, and it's not the whole story. That's just my opinion of course, but I hope it helps, or at least offers some food for thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","user":"Arkayriel","date":". 03-05-2021, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T07:10:36-08:00","id":1438118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438103#post1438103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can sympathize with the argument that even if you would be okay with having lower dot ratings, the Charm prerequisites effectively force you into hypercompetence, because even though a character with Melee 2, Excellent Strike and Dipping Swallow Defense can expect to take on a wide variety of antagonists and win, it's not going to be a very mechanically interesting character to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>And focusing on Melee is a bit of low hanging fruit with some choices about what Charms you can take at Melee 2 with three to pick from.<br /> <br /> Archery 2 only gets you access to Wise Arrow. Brawl 2 only gets you access to Fists of Iron Technique. Thrown 2 gets you Precison of the Striking Raptor and Steel Storm Mastery; but SSM requires PofSR. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, I think a solution to that is not to shrug and say &quot;ah well, I better pick Melee 5 on my freshly exalted farm girl&quot;, but to lower the stupidly high ability prerequisites. </div> </div> </div>There's also the option of returning the definitions of what each level means closer to the older versions of it; which makes 3 and 4 much easier to justify. Having moving 2 and 3 up one, and combining 4 and 5 back together, leaves room to but back in a rating between amateur and experienced proffesonial,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arkayriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438104#post1438104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She's THE daring farmgirl chosen above so many others to carry the exaltation of the greatest deity in creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that doesn't actually tell you what to give her stats wise. What Ability do you increase to show the difference between a daring farm girl and <b>the</b> daring farm girl? What would I see on the sheet that tells me the difference?<br /> <br /> If the answer to that boils down to &quot;Solar,&quot; then it doesn't have any real weight on the disconnect the OP is talking about. Because the representation of this is in the Charms and other stuff she has for being a Solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T08:38:08-08:00","id":1438126,"title":"","content":"This is all just making me think of when I held out hope that Solar Charms and the combat system in general would be nuanced enough to let you play a Jackie Chan type of character; when you're not the best fighter in the room, you could still come out on top through a mixture of dogged determination, audacity and being unconventional in ways that could outdo the better fighters when applied properly.<br /> <br /> And I don't think that's even necessarily incompatible with what many of the actual Charms do functionally.<br /> <br /> But the Ability minimums end up leaving the whole thing rather top heavy. And I know it's not exactly an easy problem to solve; reducing Ability needs might mean that characters with higher stats but lower Essence aren't being empowered, and mixing in high and low Abilities at the same Essence is probably all over the place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T09:27:06-08:00","id":1438132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438103#post1438103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I think a solution to that is not to shrug and say &amp;quot;ah well, I better pick Melee 5 on my freshly exalted farm girl&amp;quot;, but to lower the stupidly high ability prerequisites.</div> </div> </div> </div>I advocated for many years just capping the Ability minimum by the Essence minimum. Played that way in 2E for years.<br /> <br /> Nothing breaks spectacularly if you give the PCs easier access to their toys. Some niche dips become easier which opens combos and powerful options... but that doesn't damage game balance so much as make the PCs feel &quot;same-y&quot;.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1437998#post1437998\">Exoplanet's idea</a> over page is less extreme, but I don't see why that wouldn't &quot;work&quot;.<br /> <br /> Personally... I've come to like the high minimums. So long as everyone doesn't just grab a 5 so they don't have to worry about minimums, it helps force folks down different paths. YMMV.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438118#post1438118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the option of returning the definitions of what each level means closer to the older versions of it; which makes 3 and 4 much easier to justify. Having moving 2 and 3 up one, and combining 4 and 5 back together, leaves room to but back in a rating between amateur and experienced proffesonial</div> </div> </div> </div>You can. But if you are, you should probably look at the difficulty charts and the NPC stat levels and bump them up to make the PCs commensurately less powerful to match the new definitions. Which is fine if that's what you wanna do, but it sounds like work to me.<br /> <br /> (If you're going to shrug your shoulders and say that a 3 dot professional gets to pull off these elite feats because they're a protagonist, I don't see the difference between that and just saying your protagonist is an elite professional.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T12:51:02-08:00","id":1438157,"title":"","content":"I'll harp on the &quot;2e and 3e's Ability prerequisites are too high&quot; thing forever, but I also want to note that, like, it is <i>absolutely </i>not the case in 3e that if you build like the game tells you to, taking into account what the traits mean, then it won't work.<br /> <br /> Like, if you want a character whose concept is &quot;the group's main combatant&quot; and is <i>not good at fighting</i> then yes, you've set yourself up for a spot of trouble, but if there's another primary combatant then you can easily make it through the entire game contributing significantly to fights with nothing but Dex 3, Melee 2, a straight sword, and Dipping Swallow Defense and Excellent Strike. You <i>could</i> even do that as the group's primary combatant, it'd just make for much tenser combats. In 3e, at least, this works fine. If you take twos and threes in your combat stats and <i>all</i> <i>the Charms those permit</i>, then especially you will be in good shape, so long as your Attributes are complementary.<br /> <br /> But if you want to be the group's primary fighter, and you want the group to be able to fight enemies that would easily defeat elite mortal armies, then you do actually need to be that good at fighting. Part of the premise of the game is that your power doesn't <i>just </i>come from magic spells, so it's not like Vampire where you can play someone with zero combat background, take Protean and Celerity, and wreck shit left and right.<br /> <br /> In practice, the way I usually see this squared off is to assume that people get better rapidly once they exalt, and that PCs tend to be prodigies even among the exalted. You almost have to assume that anyway, given how many games involve you earning 200 XP over the course of an in-game month. So your starting ratings would reflect things that happened <i>since</i> your Exaltation as well, and you'll be able to train those things quickly during the game using Solar XP, and if you need to rationalize this you just throw in some training montages and say like &quot;Wow, what a natural! I see now what the Unconquered Sun saw in you!&quot; You don't have to do that, but if you want to, it's not really any sillier than &quot;what luck that I found this giant magic sword in that tomb!&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>Edit:</i> One last thought -- when evaluating how essential something like War Lion Stance is, do consider that, you know who else doesn't get War Lion Stance? Anyone whose combat Ability isn't Melee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 03-05-2021, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T13:08:52-08:00","id":1438158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438083#post1438083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is still ignoring the premise of the situation.<br /> <br /> We all know how to apply the (kinda lazy) tricks use to explain how supposedly everyday people have insane talents in various stories.<br /> <br /> The OP isn't asking &quot;how do I write a daring farm girl to justify having a high rating in X by adding things to the concept?&quot; The OP is asking how do you stick to the concept without expanding it and still handle the pressures in the system to build your character with an eye towards higher stats.<br /> <br /> &quot;The book is wrong to offer daring farm girl as a sample concept for a Dawn, and should have done something like farm girl with unrealized potential instead,&quot; is a valid response, but it's also focusing on the example over the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're playing a Solar, there needs to be some kind of <i>reason </i>this person was Exalted by the Unconquered Sun, made into a perfected champion set atop the throne of Creation. There has to be a reason she is a Dawn and not one of the other four castes. There are a lot of daring young farm girls out there and basically none of them get Chosen, so <i>this</i> has got to be just about the best daring young farm girl in the entire universe, right? But that's not a problem with the example; you could say exactly the same thing about &quot;bodyguard&quot; or &quot;swordsmith&quot;.<br /> <br /> You have to assume when they're giving examples that it's not just a typical person of that type, but one of the most extraordinary possible examples -- in potential, if nothing else. It's not like being a D&amp;D warlock where you're just some guy until you get spiked with cosmic power! PCs often have the <i>aesthetic</i> and <i>trappings</i> of being just some guy, but it's for the same reason shonen protagonists are often like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 03-05-2021, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T13:16:44-08:00","id":1438159,"title":"","content":"The crux of the issue is the dissonance between Supposition 1 and Supposition 2, and its effect on character creation.<br /> <br /> We all know that if you want to be <i>The Warrior of the Group</i>, you are going to want <i>The Charms</i>.<br /> You know what I mean \u2013 I mean you want to have on your character sheet the abilities to deflect punishment and dish the hurt. You want the power to face a dozen brigands and be able to fight them. You want to be able to stand and fight against monsters, ancient constructs and a Sidereal assassin that stands between you and cancelling your membership at the gym you haven't gone to in 14 years (\u2026not since <i>The Incident</i>).<br /> <br /> It's also important to remember that odds are one thing, but as any gambler or veteran roleplayer can bitterly attest: dice fall where they may \u2013 and they may just fall as a row of middle fingers.<br /> <br /> Now, yes, you are not wrong in your calculations and it is possible that I'm still carrying &quot;trauma&quot; from the previous edition which colors my expectations of lower dice pools, but it is important to stress this:<br /> Dice fall where they may \u2013 and they may just fuck you.<br /> <br /> This is obviously still true whether you're rolling a dozen dice or just a couple, but it's far, far truer the lower the dice pool is.<br /> <br /> The problem, however, is not that you can't fight decently with a low dice pool in most situations against casual opponents such as elite soldiers or First Age padlocks.<br /> The problem is that in order to be The Warrior, you do need to <i>qualify</i> for certain things.<br /> <br /> You see, elite soldiers are far from the worst thing you're going to face as a warrior exalt.<br /> You might get pitted against a Fair Folk Cataphract, for instance, and have to defend against an attack of a humble 16 dice and pass its Parry of 7 when you attack.<br /> <br /> If your dice pool is 4 (you wanted Dex 2, Melee 2, remember?) before enhancements, it's safe to say you <i>will</i>, at the very least, be blowing a full Excellency on every turn you make an attack \u2013 and you're probably going to do that to bolster your Defense every time you're attacked, as well.<br /> This means you will be spending a minimum of 8 motes every single round, before factoring in the occasional Excellent Strike.<br /> <br /> If you're wielding a mundane medium weapon, your Parry is exactly 3 before enhancements (and even with full Excellency and a good stunt, you're looking at a total of 5-6 versus 16 attack dice).<br /> <br /> I just rolled 16 dice for the hell of it and garnered 13 successes.<br /> I think it's safe to say our hero is in trouble.<br /> <br /> Yes, you won't always be facing the Fair Folk Cataphracts of the world\u2026 What do you say your odds of getting hunted down by the Wyld Hunt are? We're talking at least one to three Dragon-Blooded Immaculate monks, a legionnaire and an assassin, accompanied by a modest Size 3 battle group and you're telling me that\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4-5 dice is <i>fine</i> </div> </div> </div>No, no, it's not.<br /> <br /> I say again: you cannot just put a dot or two in Melee or Brawl and expect to be the warrior of anything.<br /> <br /> In other words, your ability to contend with the challenges the game throws at you will always come down to rolling a bunch of dice and adding effects to those dice from Charms, Stunts and whatever else.<br /> <br /> As we've already established, this brings us back to the dissonance between Supposition 1 and Supposition 2.<br /> If you want to get on the Fire and Stones Strike ride you need to be at least Melee 3 tall and if you want to survive the Fair Folk Cataphract and the shikari, you're gonna need a lot more than just that.<br /> <br /> Now, you can say that the daring young farm girl is a <i>starting </i>character and should be facing challenges appropriate to her level and get stronger and more experienced over time, raising her stats and acquiring Charms accordingly.<br /> However, what counts as a <i>starting character</i> in <b>Exalted</b>, especially when we're talking about Solar Exalted, isn't really equivalent to most other games such as D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> The daring young farm girl is a Solar, rats and drunken brigands are not worthy opponents for her. She is Exalted, she is supposed to be able to contend with elite soldiers as if they were mostly a distraction.<br /> <br /> Once again, the problem is not &quot;how can I justify taking a 5?&quot;, the problem is not &quot;how can I make an effective character without min-maxing?&quot;, the problem is not &quot;4-5 dice is fine against a single drunken brigand sometimes&quot;.<br /> <br /> The problem is that when you sit down to create a character and you try to stick to Supposition 1, you get slapped in the face by Supposition 2. So you want to account for Supposition 2, which means you have to break Supposition 1. <br /> <br /> You can, of course, pick a concept that suggests more accommodating stats \u2013 but that's not what we're talking about, and where does that leave our daring young farm girl?<br /> <br /> If putting 2 dots in Melee is <i>stretching it</i>, you are <i>not</i> going to be an efficient fighter.<br /> <br /> <b>Supposition 1:</b> I want to make a fun, interesting character and be loyal to her concept.<br /> <b>Supposition 2:</b> must be <i>this tall</i> to ride the fun train.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T13:22:08-08:00","id":1438161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438158#post1438158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're playing a Solar, there needs to be some kind of <i>reason </i>this person was Exalted by the Unconquered Sun, made into a perfected champion set atop the throne of Creation. There has to be a reason she is a Dawn and not one of the other four castes. There are a lot of daring young farm girls out there and basically none of them get Chosen, so <i>this</i> has got to be just about the best daring young farm girl in the entire universe, right? But that's not a problem with the example; you could say exactly the same thing about &quot;bodyguard&quot; or &quot;swordsmith&quot;.<br /> <br /> You have to assume when they're giving examples that it's not just a typical person of that type, but one of the most extraordinary possible examples -- in potential, if nothing else. It's not like being a D&amp;D warlock where you're just some guy until you get spiked with cosmic power! PCs often have the <i>aesthetic</i> and <i>trappings</i> of being just some guy, but it's for the same reason shonen protagonists are often like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Soaring River underwent her Exaltation when she was standing up to raiding soldiers who were burning her village down.<br /> She Exalted because of her willingness to put herself in danger in order to protect others and because her dauntless nature and willingness to act give her the <i>potential </i>for greatness, if only she had the power to achieve it.<br /> <br /> That's out daring young farm girl.<br /> <br /> And the book <i>does</i> state that you absolutely can totally be just some guy until you get hit with cosmic power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T13:26:37-08:00","id":1438163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438157#post1438157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In practice, the way I usually see this squared off is to assume that people get better rapidly once they exalt, and that PCs tend to be prodigies even among the exalted. You almost have to assume that anyway, given how many games involve you earning 200 XP over the course of an in-game month. So your starting ratings would reflect things that happened <i>since</i> your Exaltation as well, and you'll be able to train those things quickly during the game using Solar XP, and if you need to rationalize this you just throw in some training montages and say like &quot;Wow, what a natural! I see now what the Unconquered Sun saw in you!&quot; You don't have to do that, but if you want to, it's not really any sillier than &quot;what luck that I found this giant magic sword in that tomb!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That is also my reasoning when I make characters, but I think it's important to point out the dissonance between Supposition 1 and Supposition 2 and how you have to do that in order to reconcile them, and even then - it almost calls on you to purposely &quot;gimp&quot; yourself to accomodate Supposition 1.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T13:34:14-08:00","id":1438164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438161#post1438161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Soaring River underwent her Exaltation when she was standing up to raiding soldiers who were burning her village down.<br /> She Exalted because of her willingness to put herself in danger in order to protect others and because her dauntless nature and willingness to act give her the <i>potential </i>for greatness, if only she had the power to achieve it.<br /> <br /> That's out daring young farm girl.<br /> <br /> And the book <i>does</i> state that you absolutely can totally be just some guy until you get hit with cosmic power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the book says that you can be &quot;simply a person of enormous potential who has never had the opportunity to exercise it, or who is possessed by greatness of spirit&quot;, but those sound like cases where the &quot;why are my stats so good&quot; explanation writes itself, doesn't it? If feeling like your character hasn't yet transcended her origins is important to you, the thing to do there is just to start with decent attributes but crap Abilities, take a bunch of charms to offset the crap abilities, and make growing into the fullness of your power part of your character's arc. I've done that even in 1e; in 3e it's virtually painless due to having Solar XP and not needing to spend XP to raise Essence.<br /> <br /> <i>Edit:</i> Also, just to cover the math part a bit, so as not to make too many separate posts:<br /> <br /> Your minimum spend of 8 motes per round will often be a <i>maximum </i>spend as well; assuming you defend twice it gets up to 12. If you always ES, call it 9 or 13. You get 5 motes per round, so you can last <i>quite</i> a while. The character who has five attack dice before Accuracy, Solar Excellencies, and a couple Charms will totally wreck most mortal opposition, as long as they take them seriously enough to spend. Solar Excellencies and Charms, even the cheap root Charms, are practically win buttons against most things in the setting. Only comparable classes of enemy, which are rare, even have enough power to make mote efficiency an issue. And do keep in mind when looking at the numbers that players basically always stunt, but STs typically do not, or at least have full control over how much they want to stunt for the purposes of calibrating battles.<br /> <br /> Now, it's true, this character can only get her Parry up to 8. She can do that <i>easily</i>, but not every time someone attacks her, so if she's fighting people who can regularly hit Parry 8, she's probably going to want to do something other than just have a knock-down fight with them. Needless to say, those kind of adversaries are <i>uncommon</i>, so this doesn't really preclude getting into fights in general so much as being an application of the principle that you shouldn't fight vastly stronger enemies cavalierly.<br /> <br /> But...I don't see the problem with that? Are you saying you want to make a character who's not a world-class fighter, but you want her to be able to do the things world-class fighters do? Because, like, it's definitely not the case that you <i>need</i> to do those things, and your GM will just TPK the party if you don't pass the arbitrary Kung Fu Master check. But it does mean you need to plan around your actual abilities. The &quot;Wyld Hunt might kill me&quot; thing isn't an issue that only comes up with weak fighters; the Realm can muster a Hunt capable of wrecking pretty much <i>any</i> Circle below Essence 5, and in practice they don't generally do that because it makes for a bad game, and we sort of assume there's a behind-the-scenes political reason for it that makes sense. The corebook shikari aren't just on-call waiting for your party to show up; whether a Hunt is mustered, and whether you're still there when it arrives, are things you have control over as PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 03-05-2021, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T13:46:23-08:00","id":1438167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438161#post1438161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Soaring River underwent her Exaltation when she was standing up to raiding soldiers who were burning her village down.<br /> She Exalted because of her willingness to put herself in danger in order to protect others and because her dauntless nature and willingness to act give her the <i>potential </i>for greatness, if only she had the power to achieve it.<br /> <br /> That's out daring young farm girl.<br /> <br /> And the book <i>does</i> state that you absolutely can totally be just some guy until you get hit with cosmic power.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then Soaring River got stabbed to death by a bunch of raiding soldiers, because having unrealized potential when you Exalt in a dangerous situation doesn't go well. <br /> You're forgetting to account for <b>Supposition 0</b>, that the character did something worthy of Exaltation <b>and survived</b>, making it to the start of the campaign. Soaring River stood up to the raiding soldiers, Exalted , and walked away. How? Did she beat them up? Not with the 2+2 you're suggesting two posts above. Did she give a speech, rally the villagers into a fighting force, and crush the soldiers with numbers? Then she should have some pretty decent War and Performance dots to have pulled that off, yeah? Or did she draw the soldier's ire and lead them away? Better have the Defense and Disengage pools for that represented in her Dodge dots. Maybe she talked the soldiers down, convincing them of the evil of their deeds. But remember those Presence dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T14:14:07-08:00","id":1438170,"title":"","content":"Oh, something else I should say that you have to account for here is, like, if this character is meant to be the group's <i>primary</i> fighter, there's two ways that can go.<br /> <br /> The first is that, Charms notwithstanding, no one in the entire group can fight better than an experienced mortal warrior. As Exalted circles go, these guys are just not playing in the god-killing side of the pool. This is fine! It means the party is going to have a different approach than many parties do in practice, because they're likely to face physical threats with something closer to a mortal mindset than the traditional &quot;just assume you can kill anything you want&quot;, but that's a completely viable approach that makes for good games. As the countless &quot;my fights aren't challenging&quot; threads attest, fights are often <i>more </i>fun if you're weaker.<br /> <br /> The other possibility is that one (or all!) of the other PCs is playing a wilderness guide or something and goes &quot;I have some points left over, I guess I'll also be one of the greatest swordsmen in the East&quot; and they totally outclass you in a fight. People complain about this a lot, but my experience is that it's basically OK as long as the other person actually <i>wants</i> to be that good? Like, the arc you get here is extremely hype: your character starts out totally outclassed and awestruck by this incredible warrior, which makes sense because she's an inexperienced farm girl, and then they train together and gradually over the course of the game she matches and then outclasses him, because she's very focused on Melee and he's spending a lot of his Charm picks on unrelated wilderness-guide shit. I <i>love</i> that sort of thing, so the fact that the game makes it happen where you'd expect it to happen seems more like a feature than a bug to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 03-05-2021, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T14:59:36-08:00","id":1438177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438159#post1438159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, you can say that the daring young farm girl is a <i>starting </i>character and should be facing challenges appropriate to her level and get stronger and more experienced over time, raising her stats and acquiring Charms accordingly.<br /> However, what counts as a <i>starting character</i> in <b>Exalted</b>, especially when we're talking about Solar Exalted, isn't really equivalent to most other games such as D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> The daring young farm girl is a Solar, rats and drunken brigands are not worthy opponents for her. She is Exalted, she is supposed to be able to contend with elite soldiers as if they were mostly a distraction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I'm going to bow out here because I fundamentally disagree with your premise.<br /> <br /> But before I go... <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1423701#post1423701\">here's a Dex 1 Melee 0 PC taking on a dozen drunken bandits</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once again, the problem is not &amp;quot;how can I justify taking a 5?&amp;quot;, the problem is not &amp;quot;how can I make an effective character without min-maxing?&amp;quot;, the problem is not &amp;quot;4-5 dice is fine against a single drunken brigand sometimes&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> The problem is that when you sit down to create a character and you try to stick to Supposition 1, you get slapped in the face by Supposition 2. So you want to account for Supposition 2, which means you have to break Supposition 1. </div> </div> </div>The key factors you're missing from Supposition 1 are:<br /> <br /> 1a. You are playing an epic shonen protagonist.<br /> 1b. Two weeks. Five years. It literally takes two weeks of training time for a PC to train an Ability from 1 to 5. You've been Exalted for up to five years at the start of play (assuming you're playing a newly minted Solar fresh out the Jade Prison).<br /> <br /> Saying that your daring farm girl <i>who was chosen by the king of heaven to be one of his champion warriors <b>and</b> has had five years to train</i> is the greatest swordfighter in the world isn't at all incongruous.<br /> <br /> If you give your daring farm girl Melee 5, Supposition 1 remains intact. The dot rating means something. It means she's one of the greatest swordfighters to have ever lived. You're Aoi Kunieda. You're Mulan.<br /> <br /> It's not a world statement. We're not saying &quot;all farm girls are the greatest warriors in Creation&quot;. We're saying, your farm girl, if you build her that way, is the greatest warrior in Creation.<br /> <br /> Or not.<br /> <br /> Play the Wyld Hunt as something you have to run away from, and the Cataphract as a terrifying boss you need to gang up on to talk down or otherwise approach sideways.<br /> <br /> But yeah, if you want to clown on Exalted's biggest threats, you need the stats to match. You're right, Johnny Average-Warrior can't fight directional war gods single handed in a white room... why in Mela's name should they be able to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T15:20:11-08:00","id":1438179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438177#post1438177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But before I go... <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1423701#post1423701\">here's a Dex 1 Melee 0 PC taking on a dozen drunken bandits</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You keep posting this, but it's a meaningless fight. The PC has a number of unfair advantages. They're the only combatant spending WP, they're the only one stunting <i>and</i> getting high-rating stunts, they're mounted, etc. They also have a very good JB pool and a weapon set designed to turn their JB victory into a clash, meaning they're really using their JB pool as their main combat pool. Which they're apparently 4+4 in or 3+5 in, not 1+0 in. It's a great example of how to cheese a fight despite a low base to-hit pool, but not at all a practical example of play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T15:41:30-08:00","id":1438184,"title":"","content":"I'll post a more in-depth response later, but I just want to address something first:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438177#post1438177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've been Exalted for up to five years at the start of play</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Default character generation is designed to create Solars who\u2019ve been Exalted <b>for less than a year</b>. </div> </div> </div>-Core rulebook, page 126.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T16:11:49-08:00","id":1438192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438132#post1438132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I advocated for many years just capping the Ability minimum by the Essence minimum.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's certainly a way to do it. I think there can be value in varying Ability minimums. A key one should be making sure a Charm that has no reason to be high Essence isn't a trap because it's only actually/practically useful if you have the Ability rated high enough to justify the cost (though 3e tends to avoid these sorts of effects anyway).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So long as everyone doesn't just grab a 5 so they don't have to worry about minimums, it helps force folks down different paths. YMMV. </div> </div> </div>I think it's abundantly clear that for a lot of us the mileage is that they have too much impact on convincing players to grab a 5 instead of worrying about them (though BP/XP definitely contributes here).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can. But if you are, you should probably look at the difficulty charts and the NPC stat levels and bump them up to make the PCs commensurately less powerful to match the new definitions. Which is fine if that's what you wanna do, but it sounds like work to me. </div> </div> </div>Less than a 0.5 success change in average PC results isn't going to require a look at difficulty charts (any more than they already need it).<br /> <br /> The difference between a Dex 2/Larceny 2 street urchin and a Dex 5/Larceny 2 rich thief stealing for reasons and can buy lots of fancy tools, is not going to meaningfully change if the street urchin is actually the &quot;better&quot; thief at a redefined Larceny 3 for 5 dice, while still competing against the 8 dice of the talented but isn't doing it day-in and day-out for a living rich thief.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438184#post1438184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Core rulebook, page 126.</div> </div> </div> </div>In all fairness, less than a year is still plenty of time for a Solar to train a Caste/Favored ability to 5 considering how fast they do that.<br /> <br /> Of course, time isn't the only factor.<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> Something that hasn't really been touched on since Lioness said it?<br /> <br /> Is 4-5 base dice enough? Maybe, maybe not. While I'm far more sympathetic to the OP's argument than most seem to be, part of the problem with Supposition 2 (that I think a lot of people are expressing in a very roundabout way) is that how bad Supposition 2 is is extremely sensitive to your group. In one group Supposition 2 might be meaningless because they actually do run the game in a way where 4-5 dice is plenty. Another group might make Supposition 2 dominating and 4-5 dice is not enough for anything other than not being a drag on the rest of the group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T20:32:28-08:00","id":1438231,"title":"","content":"I had some time to kill, so I tried running the build <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438035#post1438035\">that habitable exoplanet proposed</a> against a squad of elite troops --Size 2, so we'll say there's around 30. In a real game I'd be using the environment as much as possible and maybe doing some intimidation or using a horse, but here I just had them stand in place and beat on each other, pretty much.<br /> <br /> I made a couple changes to the build which are worth noting:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Worse attributes, since six dice to attack might seem &quot;too good&quot;:<br /> Str 3 / Dex 2 / Sta 4<br /> App 4 / Cha 5 / Man 2<br /> Int 1 / Per 4 / Wits 4<br /> <br /> The only nonphysical one she uses here is Wits, for JB. Aside from maybe moving a point from Wits to Int, I think the only way you could get worse attributes than these without betraying the concept or taking fewer dots than you're allowed is to take physical tertiary or give her Dexterity 1.<br /> <br /> I replaced Iron Skin Concentration with Spirit Strengthens the Skin, as you can't learn the former without the latter.<br /> <br /> It is perhaps worth noting that the only non-Excellency Charms she actually got a chance to <i>use</i> were Excellent Strike, Spirit Strengthens the Skin, and (very rarely) Dipping Swallow Defense, as none of the others were relevant vs. a battle group.<br /> <br /> Caste: Melee (Supernal, lol), Awareness, Brawl, Dodge, Resistance<br /> Favored: Survival, Integrity, Athletics, Ride, Presence<br /> <br /> Willpower 8, because it seems in-character and she needs to spend her BP on <i>something</i>. This does matter though, as she tends to spend a lot for this sort of thing.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> She uses a straight sword and plate-and-chain, because there'd be no real reason for this character <i>not</i> to have heavy armour. If you're wondering where she got it, well, it's from doing stuff like this. She'd be pretty tough without it, but probably not enough to have good prospects vs. Size 2 elites. I did spend the battle group's WP, for what it's worth.<br /> <br /> I gave her a minor stunt on everything and none for the BG. I guess some people would consider that &quot;unfair&quot;, but in my experience, actual STs tend to be <i>more</i> generous, in the sense that they very rarely stunt mook piles but will usually award a major or two to a PC.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the fight is <i>excruciatingly</i> long so I'll spare you the details (unless you really want to see!), but I did it twice. The first time the battle group had dismal attack rolls but still won after 30+ rounds; however, she got it very close, down to its last two points of Magnitude on its last point of Size. Late in this battle I realized that she was <i>far</i> better off alternating between aiming and attacks than just attacking every turn, so I tried that the second time and she won very handily (basically her entire peripheral pool full) even though the BG got better rolls; having the aim bonus means she's overwhelmingly favoured to win clashes even when the BG spends WP, which helps enormously. I'm pretty sure that if you do the aiming thing, she's strongly favoured to win even if she's not willing to manifest anima.<br /> <br /> So that seems...pretty good to me? Like, if she had two other people in this fight who had even worse stats but could stick onslaught on the battle group, it'd be <i>enormous</i>. If she so much as took a Melee specialty in swords, she'd be vastly better. By Exalted warrior standards she's a joke but she can, in fact, beat a squadron of the Realm's finest without significant luck involved, which is pretty damn good for a starting character with a four-die attack pool. I feel pretty happy with where that's at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 03-06-2021, 12:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T20:43:38-08:00","id":1438235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438231#post1438231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, the fight is <i>excruciatingly</i> long so I'll spare you the details unless you really want to see, but I did it twice. The first time the battle group had dismal attack rolls but still won after 30+ rounds; however, she got it very close, down to its last two points of Magnitude on its last point of Size. Late in this battle I realized that she was <i>far</i> better off alternating between aiming and attacks than just attacking every turn, so I tried that the second time and she won very handily (basically her entire peripheral pool full) even though the BG got better rolls; having the aim bonus means she's overwhelmingly favoured to win clashes even when the BG spends WP, which helps enormously. I'm pretty sure that if you do the aiming thing, she's strongly favoured to win even if she's not willing to manifest anima.<br /> <br /> So that seems...pretty good to me? Like, if she had two other people person in this fight who had even worse stats but could stick onslaught on the battle group, it'd be <i>enormous</i>. If she so much as took a Melee specialty in swords, she'd be vastly better. By Exalted warrior standards she's a joke but she can, in fact, beat a squadron of the Realm's finest without significant luck involved, which is pretty damn good for a starting character with a four-die attack pool. I feel pretty happy with where that's at.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that when you start throwing clever tactics like aim-delay-clash around on the PC's part but not the NPC's part, you're biasing the heck out of your results. They're elites, right? Why are they attacking into an aimed delay-to-clash? They should know better than that, and should be taking their own Aim or something when she signals a clash by delaying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T20:58:20-08:00","id":1438240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438235#post1438235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel that when you start throwing clever tactics like aim-delay-clash around on the PC's part but not the NPC's part, you're biasing the heck out of your results. They're elites, right? Why are they attacking into an aimed delay-to-clash? They should know better than that, and should be taking their own Aim or something when she signals a clash by delaying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I thought about that. I'm pretty sure she'd still win if they don't clash, but it's something worth considering. The reason I didn't do it that way is because it's a <i>very weird situation.</i> Elite troops are not trained to fight a single farm girl who is remarkably tough, and she's not <i>so</i> strong that she's obviously supernatural until near the end, which would change the calculus. It's also, frankly, <i>harder</i> to use complex tactics as a group of 30 guys, even when you have Elite Drill. I give single people much more latitude to do complex manoeuvres than headless battle groups because when you're a single person you can do whatever you want, whereas a battle group can only do complex manoeuvres in accordance with its drill and leadership.<br /> <br /> There's also the fact that we are talking here about a PC versus a crew of NPC helmet-wearers. This isn't some sort of &quot;could a viking beat a samurai&quot; History Channel show, I'm trying to see what how it might play out in a game, and in an actual game I'm pretty sure I've <i>never</i> seen a battle group deliberately avoid a clash. (Of course, in an actual game she'd be doing something more complex than playing timing games, also, but.)<br /> <br /> But it's a worthwhile point and I'll see how it goes sometime if they have their Tactics Limiters unbound! A problem you run into here, though, is that their other options kind of suck. Aiming is probably the best, despite being narratively a bit ridiculous, but they benefit from it far less than she does, because their baseline is 13 dice against Defense 4-6 whereas hers (after boosting) is 10 dice, 1 success, and rerolling 1s against Defense 7, <i>and</i> she has a post-attack soak booster so, you know, if they're already going to hit her then she can offset the benefit of their aim with two motes. So it's a <i>better</i> option for them, but it's not <i>good</i>, really, and if their Initiatives ever line up on their own they're forced to take that choice without even the chance to dock her the 2 init.<br /> <br /> <i>ETA:</i> Someone might query &quot;what about full defense&quot; here, so just to field that, it's actually rather bad -- she's still more likely to hit them than not, and since they're acting simultaneously, it comes down to a coin flip whether they even get to apply their full defense against her big attack. It can't help them next round because she'll be aiming again there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 03-06-2021, 12:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T21:12:39-08:00","id":1438245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438235#post1438235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel that when you start throwing clever tactics like aim-delay-clash around on the PC's part but not the NPC's part, you're biasing the heck out of your results. They're elites, right? Why are they attacking into an aimed delay-to-clash? They should know better than that, and should be taking their own Aim or something when she signals a clash by delaying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, the elites don't know in real time what she's doing. She's not yelling delay to clash! before acting, and this is all happening very fast. Now you might say, 'but everyone has to declare down to their charms what they're doing, so the elites know she's delaying and a clash is most likely!'. Fair point, however, player's are meant to win. They're going to take that information of actions and charms and hopefully make the best tactical decisions possible every time. They've got the time as player's to sit back and make the right decisions with player knowledge, your elites don't unless you're seeking to absolutely push your players. As an example, I've done Brazilian Jiu-jitsu for years, I can frame the proper response to a crap load of submissions, sweeps and set ups, but in live rolling I still make plenty of tactical errors along with the technical ones.<br /> <br /> Edit - Of course I also understand that this is a white room fight, but those are only good for bench marking a fight any way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","user":"Arkayriel","date":". 03-06-2021, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T22:57:36-08:00","id":1438263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438159#post1438159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, you can say that the daring young farm girl is a <i>starting </i>character and should be facing challenges appropriate to her level and get stronger and more experienced over time, raising her stats and acquiring Charms accordingly.<br /> However, what counts as a <i>starting character</i> in <b>Exalted</b>, especially when we're talking about Solar Exalted, isn't really equivalent to most other games such as D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> The daring young farm girl is a Solar, rats and drunken brigands are not worthy opponents for her. She is Exalted, she is supposed to be able to contend with elite soldiers as if they were mostly a distraction.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <b>Supposition 1:</b> I want to make a fun, interesting character and be loyal to her concept.<br /> <b>Supposition 2:</b> must be <i>this tall</i> to ride the fun train.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like you're making contradictory statements for what you want out of your character, here.<br /> <br /> Do you want to:<br /> <br /> 1. Play a farm girl who only just Exalted and who, therefore, barely knows how to use a sword (but has limitless potential)? In that case, starting out, bandits will be a threat to you. This is the whole point of giving you the option to start with low melee; the statement you make by having your combat character start with low melee, few combat charms and so on is &quot;I want to slowly work my way up to invulnerable rather than starting there.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2. Play a farm girl who, after Exalting, spent a few weeks training and mastered the sword (which is a thing Exalted can do?) Then you start with higher combat stats.<br /> <br /> It doesn't seem hard. Exalted is a game that <i>allows</i> you to play an invulnerable master of war right from the starting gate. It doesn't force you to. If your character concept is &quot;I don't want to <i>start</i> as an invincible master of war&quot;, then it lets you choose to... not do that, in which case, yes, you will be able to cut your teeth on thrilling fights against gangs of bandits as you work your way up. What you're doing is like ordering the chocolate cake and then complaining that it contains chocolate.<br /> <br /> Also note that a <i>battle group</i> of bandits is something you can beat with relatively low combat stats. Killing a dozen bandits singlehandedly is an epic feat, absolutely worthy of a young Solar (especially if your character concept is &quot;barely knows how to wield a sword&quot;); if your concept is that you're just starting out and learning to use a sword, then it makes sense for it to require a little effort.<br /> <br /> (You're seriously downplaying how epic a fight like that can be. The <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qBcEOxZEoys\" target=\"_blank\">restaurant scene</a> from Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon doesn't require godly 5-across-the-board stats or earth-shattering combat charms, especially when you consider that she did take an artifact at chargen. Exalted should be able to have fights like that be thrilling - even for Solars - which means you have to be able to build Solars who can fight a teahouse full of ordinary people and have it be thrilling.)<br /> <br /> You talk about &quot;riding the fun train&quot;, but you get to indicate what you consider fun when you choose your concept. If you consider wasting time fighting bandits to be beneath you, perhaps you should make a character concept which can effortlessly dispatch bandits? A farm girl who barely knows how to use a sword and who has never taken a life before is <i>not that</i>, so I don't get why you're talking about making one and then complaining that the results are unfun.<br /> <br /> Finally, it <i>is</i> worth pointing out that Solars generally - not always, but generally - Exalt in a caste that reflects things they are already skilled in. A farm girl who has never touched a weapon before and whose combat experience consists of a few friendly brawls with other kids in town is absolutely a valid Dawn concept for someone who wants to start slow, but isn't exactly the iconic one. It's <i>supported</i>, but it feels like you're taking that one-off mention that it's an option and then turning around and demanding that it play the same way as the legendary warrior who was already nearly unbeatable before they Exalted, and obviously that's not going to be the case.<br /> <br /> (Obviously which version you play also requires some understanding from your group and ST - if you don't build your Dawn as a combat monster and the person next to you does, well, unless you're interested in playing their young apprentice or something you might be unhappy. But that's a matter of reconciling everyone's character concepts and figuring out what you expect out of the game as a group.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 03-11-2021, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T16:49:38-08:00","id":1438841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438167#post1438167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And then Soaring River got stabbed to death by a bunch of raiding soldiers, because having unrealized potential when you Exalt in a dangerous situation doesn't go well.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to forget that the massive stat difference between unexalted human and an exalted one is a thing. And not all of those Abilities and Attributes are gained during the following year. Some get applied on the spot. It is <i>not</i> implausible for the newly exalted person to suddenly start using a martial style that has been forgotten for hundreds of years, or show swordmanship on competence level suggesting hundreds of years of prior experience. Even if said person never learned any martial arts or never held a sword before. Those things also happen. Suddenly, using that sword, for some unexplained reason just seems natural and easy.<br /> <br /> That's one point most people here seem to forget. The switch from unexalted to exalted is <i>not</i> slow and gradual - it is a moment you erupt with strength you didn't have before. Janest and <i>Strawmaiden</i> Janest almost certainly do <b>not</b> have the same stats.<br /> <br /> That alone is enough to explain away the conflict between those two suppositions from OPs post.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T12:42:21-08:00","id":1438999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438167#post1438167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-having unrealized potential when you Exalt in a dangerous situation doesn't go well.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The book</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Solars are often men and women who have already accomplished great things and displayed excellence in some discipline or other. <b>This isn\u2019t universal\u2014sometimes a Solar is simply a person of enormous potential who has never had the opportunity to exercise it, or who is possessed of greatness of spirit.</b><br /> - <b>Often the Solar finds herself facing a difficult or insurmountable trial of some sort, and Exaltation grants her the power necessary to survive or triumph.</b><br /> - [Exaltation] has uplifted princes and paupers, <b>children</b> and great-grandfathers, savants and sell-swords, saints and assassins</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I'm a little confused here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","user":"Maseiken","date":". 03-10-2021, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T14:09:05-08:00","id":1439026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438235#post1438235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel that when you start throwing clever tactics like aim-delay-clash around on the PC's part but not the NPC's part, you're biasing the heck out of your results. They're elites, right? Why are they attacking into an aimed delay-to-clash? They should know better than that, and should be taking their own Aim or something when she signals a clash by delaying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so this is actually very simple. Below are the stats of a dawn farmhand girl who's a bit better than her friends with her fists.<br /> <br /> 4 Str<br /> 3 Dex<br /> 4 Sta<br /> 3 Wits<br /> <br /> 2 Brawl (specialty bare fists)<br /> 2 Awareness<br /> 2 Resistance<br /> <br /> Charms:<br /> Awareness/Brawl Excellency<br /> Fists of Iron Technique<br /> Durability of Oak Meditation<br /> Ox Body Technique<br /> <br /> <br /> This is her statline compared to the statline of a size 1 battlegroup of bandits, assuming she's using charms. Numbers will be green when the Solar has a greater value, and blue when that value is greater by at least double.<br /> <br /> 05 || <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">10</span> Join Battle<br /> 07 || <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">15</span> Withering Attack<br /> 12 || <span style=\"color:#008000\">16</span> Damage<br /> 07 || <span style=\"color:#008000\">11</span> Decisive Attack<br /> 02 || <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">05</span> Defense<br /> 07 || 06 Soak<br /> 08 || <span style=\"color:#008000\">10</span> Health Levels<br /> <br /> <br /> It seems to me that this Solar can at least plausibly beat a group of bandits, with her bare hands, and wearing nothing but the rags on her back.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also feel like this might come up but, from the corebook on page 35 &quot;If an Exalt uses up all her store of Essence, she becomes little more than a mortal for a time.&quot; A Solar who isn't using charms is just a mortal who doesn't suffer from sepsis and lives to be 1,000.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 03-10-2021, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T22:34:03-08:00","id":1439382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1438999#post1438999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I'm a little confused here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having that potential be still unrealized, after exalting, when you kinda sorta really need that realized potential <i>now</i>. That's dangerous. And that's what OP is talking about playing. <br /> Exalting in a dangerous situation and getting that whammy of suddenly-realized potential handed to you? Sure, now you're probably fine. But that's not what OP is talking about playing. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> DrLoveMonkey, what do relative stats and size 1 bandit groups have to do with the tactics of elite cav and biasing combats via uneven tactical intelligence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T06:00:22-08:00","id":1439431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1439382#post1439382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DrLoveMonkey, what do relative stats and size 1 bandit groups have to do with the tactics of elite cav and biasing combats via uneven tactical intelligence?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was more responding to the sub thread that a Solar needs badass stats to survive, if they don\u2019t have them then a group of bandits will shank them before their story even starts. If you\u2019re just a mediocre fighter who gets surrounded by a bunch of bandits and told to hand over what few coins you have in exchange for your life...you respond by smashing the entire group of armed thieves into the dirt with your bare hands, and it\u2019s not even close. <br /> <br /> You have unrealized potential, you\u2019re only average for a brawler but you could be a lot more. Until then though, you\u2019re not in danger because some random thugs on the street want to shank you, your Solar might outclasses them by a mile and a half. <br /> <br /> What about comparing to elite soldiers though?<br /> <br /> 10 || 10 Join Battle<br /> 12 || 15 Withering Attack<br /> 13 || 16 Damage<br /> 12 || 11 Decisive Attack<br /> 05 || 05 Defense<br /> 11 || 06 Soak<br /> 08 || 10 Health Levels<br /> <br /> <br /> That\u2019s actually not that bad either. Matches or beats them in every catagory except losing out by one die on decisive attacks and 5 on soak. <br /> <br /> Again, this is an unarmed farmhand with no armor, and they match a squad of elite warriors blow for blow and then some, with only two Brawl and three charms. At which point if your character is the farmhand with unrealized potential, you can start training and growing in power as a character, your fights moving from schooling street thugs and monstrocities to battling a deathlord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T14:30:55-08:00","id":1439519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1439382#post1439382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having that potential be still unrealized, after exalting, when you kinda sorta really need that realized potential <i>now</i>. That's dangerous. And that's what OP is talking about playing.<br /> Exalting in a dangerous situation and getting that whammy of suddenly-realized potential handed to you? Sure, now you're probably fine. But that's not what OP is talking about playing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all relative, but not really? Charms make way more of a difference than abilities. The standard you've set here isn't for an effective combatant with low abilities, but a starting character that can survive an exaltation despite having low abilities. That is extremely achievable.<br /> <br /> In the first place, there's plenty of combat situations that would be exaltation-worthy to a mortal but utterly achievable for an exalt with low ability ratings, as DrLoveMonkey is illustrating. But beyond that, the non-combat solutions break the entire assumption.<br /> <br /> Charisma 3/Presence 3 could be a server in a tea-house or just a friendly, outgoing villager who likes talking to people. She's unusually magnetic, but not a renowned figure. She's being menaced by a Size 2 unit of elite soldiers. Enough to have destroyed her village, threaten her life, and make all seem lost. She Exalts.<br /> <br /> She would like to intimidate them into letting her leave. She's at full Anima, so the threat has enough legitimacy to be attempted.<br /> With just two charms, Tiger's Dread Symmetry and Listener-Swaying Argument, she's rolling effectively 12-15(+1 Success) vs Resolve 4-7 (Depending on whether an Intimacy is resisting them). 13-16 for a Dawn.<br /> This isn't guaranteed, but it's far from hopeless. Most rampaging jerks wouldn't really have the second intimacy necessary to Decision Point out of it.<br /> <br /> Blinding Battle Feint is one charm at Stealth 3 that will get her out of that situation even easier.<br /> <br /> Being pursued and cornered by an Abyssal hunter's bloodthirsty hounds is absolutely an Exaltation-worthy situation. Monkey Leap Technique lets you jump clear over a twenty foot wall. You can literally jump over the wall you were backed up against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","user":"Maseiken","date":". 03-12-2021, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T16:34:50-08:00","id":1439536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1439519#post1439519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charisma 3/Presence 3 could be a server in a tea-house or just a friendly, outgoing villager who likes talking to people.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is precisely the OP's stated problem though.<br /> <br /> Presence 3 isn't a server in a tea-house, or just the local friendly townsperson. Presence 3 is an exception individual that's better than most professionals. A Presence 3 server is the best tipped server in the most prestigious tea house in a major city. A Presence 3 townsperson is probably the most influence person in the town even if they're not officially in charge of anything because they're the most persuasive person that town has seen in living memory.<br /> <br /> When you cut these down to Presence 1 or 2 (or whatever Ability) and suddenly don't qualify for all the cool Charms that would let you justify your Exaltation... it gets weirder. A Solar might be able to train up to Presence 3 and those Charms in a very short amount of time, but that doesn't mean they were that at the time of their Exaltation.<br /> <br /> That's why a bunch of us want to slash the Ability minimums drastically so there's more Ability 1 and 2 Charms so players can take Listener-Swaying Argument and Tiger's Dread Symmetry as starting Presence Charms without having to justify Presence 3 as Presence 3 is written in the book.<br /> <br /> It's why I'd love to see the description of Abilities adjusted so that 3s aren't already exception in your field ratings (and it deal with straining the imagination of &quot;exceptional, more exceptional, and even more more exceptional&quot; when trying to figure out what 3 vs 4 vs 5 looks like).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T01:55:56-08:00","id":1439619,"title":"","content":"It seems like that would do odd things symbolically to the idea that Ability Charms are outgrowths of at least mild unenhanced competence (represented by Ability minima). The current design does seem to place value on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T04:01:52-08:00","id":1439626,"title":"","content":"Except 1 dot in an Ability <b>is</b> mild competence. 2 dots is as much competence as most people that use that Ability for a living will ever attain. 3 dots is already an exceptional level of competence.<br /> <br /> I would argue that it's more likely that the current design is just following the previous two editions of design and didn't rethink Ability minimums while also rewriting how Abilities were defined (from1e's more WoD-style definitions, to 2e's closer intentions to 3e but more vague with more room for interpretation), Charms trees tending to get to 3 fast or just start there made more sense back when a 3 was described as being good at something, and 4 was exceptional, as it meant starting at 3 at anything your character was focused on was easy to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T06:09:41-08:00","id":1439635,"title":"","content":"You know, there\u2019s a distinct possibility that skill doesn\u2019t always go <i>recognized</i> in Creation; sometimes the guy who\u2019s known around town for his business acumen is a hack who got lucky a few times, while the woman who works the tea house can run numbers in her head smoothly enough, yet the people who own the place never even notice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T14:09:12-08:00","id":1439717,"title":"","content":"Sorta? It's not like I was giving examples of people that would have any widespread recognition of their talent.<br /> <br /> Given that Abilities are trained skills that require time and effort to develop (however accelerated for Exalts), it's very difficult to say that you developed a 3+ in something before Exalting and somehow nobody's noticed this. Recognition isn't inherently global or anything. Being the best tipped tea server at the best tea-house in Nexus doesn't mean everyone in Nexus recognizes you, let alone Creation, but your employer and/or fellow employees certainly know you're the best they know off. Some of the major players in Nexus at least know your name and face (because it's Nexus and it pays to be aware of the people around you even if you don't actually care about them emotionally). But you can easily walk down the street and nobody would know who you are, or what your greatest talents are. Nobody in Gem is aware of your existence.<br /> <br /> The way the book describes traits, characters that go under the radar completely unintentionally are best represented by high Attributes and low Abilities. An Intelligence 5/Bureaucracy 1 character could easily be missed as a server that helps the owners with the books a bit, even though their genius is what actually keeps the business in the black because they easily outperform an Intelligence 2/Bureaucracy 2 manager who's better trained and more experienced in running a business.<br /> <br /> When you try to say that somehow you have a 3+ and nobody at all realizes it, it quickly strains plausibility (unless you hand-wave away how the books describe the traits, which is sensible but not really the point). At 3 you're better than the vast majority of people that will ever rely on this Ability for a living.<br /> <br /> A shepherd that's developed Thrown 3 with a sling fending off predators might have done so via innate aptitude and all, and nobody saw the real world experience training happen, but people are going to notice that shepherd hasn't lost an animal while taking them grazing in years, while everyone else loses a few each season. They're going to be curious, even if they don't buy the modest answer of &quot;I practice with my sling a lot,&quot; and if they try to spy never see more than... skill with a sling and attention to the animals.<br /> <br /> Recognition isn't binary. The higher the Ability rating, the harder it is to say there's zero recognition at all.<br /> <br /> And, of course, Creation has things watching and recognizing that aren't just other humans... or these people wouldn't be Exalting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T18:22:46-08:00","id":1439758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1439717#post1439717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why a bunch of us want to slash the Ability minimums drastically so there's more Ability 1 and 2 Charms so players can take Listener-Swaying Argument and Tiger's Dread Symmetry as starting Presence Charms without having to justify Presence 3 as Presence 3 is written in the book.<br /> <br /> It's why I'd love to see the description of Abilities adjusted so that 3s aren't already exception in your field ratings (and it deal with straining the imagination of &quot;exceptional, more exceptional, and even more more exceptional&quot; when trying to figure out what 3 vs 4 vs 5 looks like).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't disagree particularly with those adjustments. My original point was just that you really don't need optimized abilities ratings to Survive Exaltation scenarios (the premise I was responding to.<br /> The conversation over how competent the ratings are and how competent starting characters should be is a separate one. Personally I don't think 3 dots is a big deal fame-wise, but I guess it depends on how notable a 'recognised veteran or expert' is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T21:56:54-08:00","id":1439784,"title":"","content":"I feel like the one point no is bringing up is that the default exalted CC represents at least a year or two of being exalted. Exalted also learn much faster then mortals. They pick up abilities, skills, and strength themselves innate with more then just charms much faster. I'd definitely use a weaker CC generation to represent someone who was just exalted and a slower learning curve for mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T22:10:48-08:00","id":1439785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1439784#post1439784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd definitely use a weaker CC generation to represent someone who was just exalted and a slower learning curve for mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s actually one in the book already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T22:19:13-08:00","id":1439787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1439785#post1439785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s actually one in the book already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I ask where it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T22:23:24-08:00","id":1439788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1439758#post1439758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My original point was just that you really don't need optimized abilities ratings to Survive Exaltation scenarios (the premise I was responding to.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what I'm saying, is that with the way the books define Abilities, the 3s necessary to have the Charms to make it out of the Exaltation is optimizing, even if not maximally so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The conversation over how competent the ratings are and how competent starting characters should be is a separate one. </div> </div> </div>But the conversation isn't really either? It's how competent the ratings are interacts with how competent certain concepts should be vs. how competent the system pressures them to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1439784#post1439784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the one point no is bringing up is that the default exalted CC represents at least a year or two of being exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was brought up. Post #35 directly cites the book, and that starting level Solars have only been Exalted for less than a year.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T22:29:22-08:00","id":1439789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1439788#post1439788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This was brought up. Post #35 directly cites the book, and that starting level Solars have only been Exalted for less than a year.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still more then enough time to gain a bunch of abilities and attributes. Maybe CC isn't the best way to look at it but looking at it. An exalt can learn favored/caste skills in days, non-favored skills in weeks and attributes in months and you can learn them concurrently. And while pcs and nps are stated differently. it does show that an exalt with 11 months and someone who needs to survive would be able to use that time to learn as much as they could to survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 03-14-2021, 01:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T05:31:02-07:00","id":1439803,"title":"","content":"The problem in question isn't, &quot;can you make a character that through a combination of previous life skills, Exaltation, and some time as an Exalt, that justifies having high stats?&quot; So focusing on things like how long a new character is presumed to have been an Exalt isn't really that helpful.<br /> <br /> The problem in question is, &quot;why does the game suggest that it's valid to make characters that haven't yet invested into post-Exaltation training, but then pressure you into having stats beyond what that concept would suggest by locking things (mostly Charms) behind high ratings?&quot;<br /> <br /> There is a side tangent on the issue of surviving the earliest parts of becoming a Solar (the Exaltation itself, and the time period directly after) before the character would start getting some of those char-gen resources. Because that's part of the issue with the narrative of the &quot;person that just Exalted takes advantage of Exalted training times to boost their stats quickly,&quot; in that they have to survive a period between not having those stats and the time it takes to get them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T06:53:21-07:00","id":1439806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1439536#post1439536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is precisely the OP's stated problem though.<br /> <br /> Presence 3 isn't a server in a tea-house, or just the local friendly townsperson. Presence 3 is an exception individual that's better than most professionals. A Presence 3 server is the best tipped server in the most prestigious tea house in a major city. A Presence 3 townsperson is probably the most influence person in the town even if they're not officially in charge of anything because they're the most persuasive person that town has seen in living memory.<br /> <br /> When you cut these down to Presence 1 or 2 (or whatever Ability) and suddenly don't qualify for all the cool Charms that would let you justify your Exaltation... it gets weirder. A Solar might be able to train up to Presence 3 and those Charms in a very short amount of time, but that doesn't mean they were that at the time of their Exaltation.<br /> <br /> That's why a bunch of us want to slash the Ability minimums drastically so there's more Ability 1 and 2 Charms so players can take Listener-Swaying Argument and Tiger's Dread Symmetry as starting Presence Charms without having to justify Presence 3 as Presence 3 is written in the book.<br /> <br /> It's why I'd love to see the description of Abilities adjusted so that 3s aren't already exception in your field ratings (and it deal with straining the imagination of &quot;exceptional, more exceptional, and even more more exceptional&quot; when trying to figure out what 3 vs 4 vs 5 looks like).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with lowering the Ability minimums. <br /> <br /> I think it might be possible / desirable to interpret Ability 3 as a bit lower than you're doing, while following the description in the book. It says &quot;The character\u2019s training in the Ability surpasses the competence expected even of professionals, marking her as an elite or veteran in her field.&quot; A veteran soldier is better than the average professional soldier, but if you're going to war, you're not at all surprised to see a veteran soldier. I think 3 can be &quot;noticeably better than the average professional&quot; but not &quot;in towns, the best in living memory&quot; - like, if the town has ten people who reach a professional level at something and two are notably better than the others, those two might have 3 dots. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T09:18:39-07:00","id":1439822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1439803#post1439803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem in question isn't, &quot;can you make a character that through a combination of previous life skills, Exaltation, and some time as an Exalt, that justifies having high stats?&quot; So focusing on things like how long a new character is presumed to have been an Exalt isn't really that helpful.<br /> <br /> The problem in question is, &quot;why does the game suggest that it's valid to make characters that haven't yet invested into post-Exaltation training, but then pressure you into having stats beyond what that concept would suggest by locking things (mostly Charms) behind high ratings?&quot;<br /> <br /> There is a side tangent on the issue of surviving the earliest parts of becoming a Solar (the Exaltation itself, and the time period directly after) before the character would start getting some of those char-gen resources. Because that's part of the issue with the narrative of the &quot;person that just Exalted takes advantage of Exalted training times to boost their stats quickly,&quot; in that they have to survive a period between not having those stats and the time it takes to get them.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the second problem I agree with it being a problem. I thought they were going to lower ability ratings but you can't go more then E2 to in a few cases E3 without everything being ability 5. I was hoping for for something more gradual with other exalts.<br /> <br /> On the side tangent I do have to point out that surviving and repeatedly preforming those actions is a way to get better at them. The more a person climbs through harsh, terrain, uses his charm to off-set his opponent, and craft more tools for the next fight is a way to build up more competency in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 03-14-2021, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T10:03:11-07:00","id":1439830,"title":"","content":"Reminder that plenty of classical heroes <i>did</i> start as just farmboys aside from being demigods, with their parentage being considered all the justification needed for their prowess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T14:51:33-07:00","id":1439902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1439806#post1439806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A veteran soldier is better than the average professional soldier, but if you're going to war, you're not at all surprised to see a veteran soldier.</div> </div> </div> </div>War is also a bit of an outlier as it concentrates professionals in one place at one time, and every side in the war is (generally) bringing the best fighters they have to the conflict.<br /> <br /> A large chunk of people in creation need to travel at least a day round-trip to get to a blacksmith, and another large chunk living in a place with just one blacksmith. Finding &quot;elite&quot; blacksmiths isn't as expected outside of the biggest industrial centers in Creation because there just isn't a reason to have enough of them in one place unless that place has a lot of smithing needing done. And most highly skilled individuals are going to have some social pressure to set up shop where their skill can benefit them the most.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think 3 can be &quot;noticeably better than the average professional&quot; but not &quot;in towns, the best in living memory&quot; - like, if the town has ten people who reach a professional level at something and two are notably better than the others, those two might have 3 dots. </div> </div> </div>While the game might be better if that was how the phrasing was handled, I don't think that really gets to the &quot;veteran&quot; or &quot;elite&quot; aspect of the text. Those two are far more likely to have a specialty or higher Attributes or more Willpower than actually have a 3 based on descriptions. After all, a 4 is someone so good that rich people send their 3 rated expensive private attendants to 4s when there's something so special a 3 can't hack it. That doesn't really mesh well with 1/5 professionals being a 3 on either side of how skilled that descriptively makes them.<br /> <br /> This goes back to 1e (and the WoD) where 3 was above average compared to the general population, but average for a working professional, 4 was exceptional/elite/etc., leaving 5 to be the &quot;genius&quot; rating. 3e eliminated the old 2 between amateur and professional, and it compresses things oddly from a descriptive stance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1439822#post1439822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the side tangent I do have to point out that surviving and repeatedly preforming those actions is a way to get better at them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book actually talks about this when pointing out that training times are supposed to be flexible, and that &quot;learning on the job&quot; is actually a sub-optimal approach compared to a mixture of structured and practical training (as well as the assumed time spent on training). While it doesn't really matter to a caste/favored Ability, since you can double the training times on those and still not really impact how insanely fast they train up, it does mean things like Attributes would progress much slower if you're just increasing them through survival applications of your skills.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1439830#post1439830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reminder that plenty of classical heroes <i>did</i> start as just farmboys aside from being demigods, with their parentage being considered all the justification needed for their prowess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminder: we know, but that's not the point. The point is that the books say you can play a character that justifies their prowess through hard work, not having it divinely handed to them, but then doesn't really make that as viable as this sort of approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T01:05:28-07:00","id":1440159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1437939-my-kind-of-opposite-problem-with-something-else-in-chargen?p=1439830#post1439830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reminder that plenty of classical heroes <i>did</i> start as just farmboys aside from being demigods, with their parentage being considered all the justification needed for their prowess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's taken care of by charms, like the excellency.<br /> <br /> A Solar swordsman with dex 3 melee 2 is a greater swordsman than the greatest mortal who ever lived. The mortal has 11 dice, the Solar has 11, and more charms beside that that grant additional abilities. <br /> <br /> Which is pretty amazing. Somebody with just average professional skill with a blade and slightly above average dexterity suddenly outpaces the most legendary and storied mortal as soon as they get their exaltation, without even changing any dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 03-16-2021, 04:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T00:37:21-07:00","id":1440330,"title":"","content":"I feel like there's an elegant solution to be had when you consider 2 points: 1) The sheet is not necessarily the character and 2) Celestial Exaltations carry flashes of memories and thus conceivably skills through their reincarnations.<br /> <br /> When Soaring River parries and knocks the raid leader to the ground with a stick, it feels like she has done it 10,000 times. The captain stares up at her, awestruck by the blazing mark on her brow but also that same mark on the scores of glowing figures behind her. (This is also a pre-established Exalted trope seen on pages 21 and 24 of the <b>Tale of the Visiting Flare</b>.)<br /> <br /> Soaring River can have the meager dots from Supposition 1, AND her sheet can have the high dots needed for Supposition 2. This is possible because not all the dots have to represent <i>her</i> stats. The sheet can also represent the long line of Solar behemoth-slayers that now inhabit the daring farm girl.<br /> <br /> If you really want to, you could ask a Storyteller to let you run 2 separate sheets: one for Aang and one for the Avatar state. Mechanically, you might switch based on a particular Anima level or when your Defining Intimacy is at stake. You may have inadvertently hit on a new and interesting style of play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1925-toroid","name":"Toroid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T22:17:02-07:00","id":1440908,"title":"","content":"I do think it's worth reiterating that while playing the farmgirl Dawn is an <i>option</i>, it's not really the default assumption for Solar Exalted (who are generally Exalted in a caste because they're already peerless experts in what that caste does.) Even a farmgirl Dawn is likely to eg. be the best arm-wrestling brawler in her village, or was taught to hunt and use a bow by her uncle until nobody in town is a match for her, or her father was a soldier who made her practice with a quarterstaff every day or something - ala the Luke Skywalker shooting womp-rats example someone mentioned above.<br /> <br /> Exalting in something that you genuinely didn't do before at all - or even something you were merely competent at - isn't really central to the Solar theme. It might make more sense for eg. Sidereals, so perhaps they should have lower ability minimums for intro charms to fit the theme of &quot;this is my destiny so as a total newbie Sidereal, the flow of Fate guides me even if I've never trained a day in my life before.&quot; When you start talking about a Solar starting with 1 or 2 in the Ability that is central to their concept, though, it starts to feel like you're forcing in a concept that is somewhat unusual for a Solar. Which is fine! Unusual characters can be cool.<br /> <br /> But they're also going to play a bit differently, and the mechanics may not provide full support for doing everything you would normally <i>expect</i> (because you're not playing the expected character) - eg. the Dawn whose highest combat skill is a 1 would be like Allison Ruth from <i>Kill Six Billion Demons</i>, and would need to rely on others a bit until they've found a teacher or time to train or the like. To me, that's what you're asking to play when you start with low or merely average skills in your main focus as a Solar.<br /> <br /> If you want to say &quot;my Exaltation granted me peerless skill even though I had no prior training!&quot;, well... just start with at least 3 in your main combat skill, then?<br /> <br /> But I'm not understanding what people are asking for if they want to start with Melee 1 or 2, <i>and</i> also be an amazing Solar warrior. Solar excellence comes from their skill - that is to say, you have to actually be above average at what you do in order to get much out of it. For a Solar, starting with Melee 1 or 2 literally means, thematically, that you want to start as someone who hasn't yet grasped the pinnacle necessary to draw on their Solar prowess, and whose story is therefore going to start low-key as they struggle to unlock it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}